# =============================================================================
# Dream-Waver — root .gitignore
#
# Multi-stack repo: Next.js (apps/web), Go orchestrator (services/orchestrator),
# Python sidecar (services/dreamapi-sidecar), Rust sandbox (services/sandbox),
# slide-templates, proto bindings. Each section below names what it protects.
#
# Patterns are ordered:
#   1. Secrets (highest priority — never accidentally commit credentials)
#   2. Language-specific build outputs / dependencies
#   3. Tooling caches (lint / test / type-check)
#   4. Editor + OS noise
#   5. Project-specific local artifacts
#   6. Negate rules (LAST — they re-include things prior rules would skip)
# =============================================================================

# ─── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.development.local
.env.production.local
.env.test.local
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
.dreamapi/

# ─── Go ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# **/bin catches `go build -o ./bin/foo`; **/dist catches release tarballs.
# vendor/ catches `go mod vendor` output — we use modules, not vendored deps.
**/bin/
**/dist/
*.test
*.out
go.work
go.work.sum
vendor/
# Built binaries that sometimes end up next to source during `go build`
services/orchestrator/cmd/server/server
services/sandbox/cmd/sandbox/sandbox

# ─── Rust ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
target/
**/target/
Cargo.lock.bak

# ─── Node.js / Next.js / TypeScript ──────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
.turbo/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/cache
.yarn/install-state.gz
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
.parcel-cache/
.swc/

# ─── Python (sidecar) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.venv/
venv/
env/
.uv/
.python-version
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pdm.toml
pip-wheel-metadata/
*.egg-info/

# ─── Test / coverage outputs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# ─── Editor / IDE state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.#*
\#*\#
.history/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
.zed/

# ─── OS junk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ─── Backup / patch files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# ─── Logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ─── SQLite (local DBs from sidecar / open-design clones) ────────────────────
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.db-journal

# ─── Local Docker overrides ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yaml

# ─── Generated artifacts (per-deploy / per-run output) ───────────────────────
# Renders + slide artifacts the orchestrator drops in working dirs. Real
# deliverables live in object storage; on-disk copies are throwaway.
*.pptx
*.pdf
.tmp/
tmp/
/workspace/
storage_local/
sandbox_local/
# open-design daemon's local data dir (if a sibling clone exists)
.od/
# Local AI image cache the orchestrator writes (configurable via env)
ai-images/
.ai-cache/

# ─── Claude Code — per-developer state ───────────────────────────────────────
# .claude/ holds settings, agent transcripts, worktrees that the Claude Code
# CLI creates locally. These are developer-specific, not part of the repo.
.claude/

# ─── Negate rules — re-include what prior rules would skip ───────────────────
# Generated protobuf bindings live under /proto and ARE committed
# (tracking generated code keeps `go generate` optional during checkout).
# The negate must come AFTER the broad rules above.
!proto/**/*.go
!proto/**/*.rs

# dev symlink to the main checkout install (dir-only node_modules/ rule misses symlinks)
apps/web/node_modules
